  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low, deliberate four-beat basilisk stalk with wide planted palms, visible shoulder and thigh movement, a steady armored back and a raised spiked tail. The scramble lengthens and quickens the steps without bouncing.",
    "attack": "Four feet brace a short coil and forceful straight-ahead head/body lunge, then recover. The source mouth keeps its natural gape; fused mouth tissue is not pulled apart to imply an independent jaw snap.",
    "death": "The heavy belly lowers forward to the ground, the head relaxes low, the limbs spread gently and the centered spiked tail relaxes behind the body before a still hold."
